From 3c27303d1cbb43b4041c1dde335c33487c48ed9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:58:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(deepseek_v4_1): reuse indexer key tiles across row pairs
 and split decode indexer across TP

Rationale:
- In dense indexer_score_v41 (layers 2, 8, 14, 20), each CTA previously scored one query row (grid = (ctas, rows)) and loaded its own 64-position key+scale tiles from KPool/KScale, even when consecutive rows belonged to the same request and read the same pages.
- At decode, the replicated indexer also scored all batch rows on every TP rank, whereas sequence-parallel prefill already splits indexer rows across TP ranks via SPRows.

Changes:
- Pair consecutive rows in dense indexer_score_v41 (grid = (ctas, ceildiv(rows, 2))). When a CTA's tiles for row0 and row1 share identical page-table entries and tile coverage, load each 64-key tile once into shared memory and score both rows' 32 heads together in a single [64, 128] x [64, 128] mma_gemm_blockscaled call; otherwise fall back per row.
- In DeepseekV41TileLangAttention._forward, split target-model decode indexing (_index_query and forward_mqa top-k selection) across TP ranks via sp_prefill.SPRows(rows, tp_size, tp_rank) whenever tp_size > 1 and rows >= tp_size (gated by VLLM_DS41_DECODE_INDEX_SPLIT=1, default enabled) and all-gather the selected 512 top-k indices per row.
- Allow select_rows to cache each rank's decode page-table slice (_ds41_index_pages) across index layers sharing the same indexer cache group when split is active, and guard _index_query when a trailing rank's split slice has 0 real rows.

Quality implications:
- Bit-for-bit identical BF16 scores and top-k indices on dense and candidate index layers.

Tests:
- pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang.py -k 'indexer or pages'
- pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py
